  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Skill Requirements**\n\nI\'m currently dissecting the skill check section of the guidelines. I\'ve noted the absence of specific skill designations like \"html/css/migration\". Therefore, I\'m cross-referencing this with available skills. Specifically, I\342\200\231m eliminating `firebase-integration`, `gemini-api`, and `image-generation` because they seem irrelevant to the task. My focus is on identifying the precise skills needed.\n\n\n**Identifying Relevant Code**\n\nI\'ve determined that no specific skills are active for this migration. Upon reviewing the provided code, I now see two HTML files, one with a table and styles, another with JavaScript, and an image, as well as several Rich Text formatted entries that clarify their purpose. The code details legacy HTML applications with embedded JavaScript and `localStorage`, created for a Venezuelan logistics company \"DISGLOBAL,\" tracking POS terminals.\n\n\n**Examining Project Structure**\n\nI\'m now diving into the React application\'s structure. I\'m focusing on `/package.json` to understand dependencies. The plan is to list the core tabs and boards within the original HTML. I\'m examining the files provided to map out the application\'s functionality for this migration.\n\n\n**Mapping Application Features**\n\nI\'m now outlining the application\'s key functionalities. I see that **GESTION GENERAL** handles bulk serial number processing with extensive filtering and status management, including local storage persistence. **CASILLERO** focuses on item-specific details like accessories, technician delivery tracking, and delivery controls. These features and their controls will be crucial for the migration\'s success.\n\n\n**Defining Feature Components**\n\nI\'m now detailing more of the functionalities. I see that **HACER ENVIO** handles external shipment registration, along with the records. **CRUCE DE SERIALES** includes validator file import, serial list parsing, matching displays, and various actions. The **EQUIPOS ENVIADOS** section stores shipment history. Lastly, **MODELOS** manages POS terminal model prefixes. I\'ll continue to examine all the functionalities to fully understand the features.\n\n\n"
