  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Initiating Data Configuration**\n\nI\'m currently working on creating `/src/data.ts`. My aim is to establish a foundational configuration for initial model definitions, alongside a pre-set list of serials, should local storage be employed. This setup will streamline access to essential model and serial data at the project\'s onset.\n\n\n**Replicating Javascript Behavior**\n\nI\'ve successfully replicated the behavior of the HTML by initializing storage as empty. Now, I\'m examining the model list from the user\'s Javascript, specifically the `defaultModelos` object. This list includes a wide range of devices. I\'ll need to accurately represent this model data.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will create `/src/data.ts` to host the initial mock data of POS models, initial demo serials, and auxiliary styling/mapping tables. This separates static data definitions from the core React UI logic and maximizes system maintainability."
