  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Addressing Navigation**\n\nI\'ve altered the navigation container, implementing `flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 pb-3 border-b border-slate-900`. This should eliminate the horizontal scrollbar issue for the navigation tabs, as requested. I focused on making the navigation display effectively within the available space.\n\n\n**Enhancing Visual Design**\n\nI\'ve been meticulously updating the visual design, and I\'m quite pleased with the results. I\'ve been giving careful thought to how the elements will appear and feel to the end-user. I\'ve refactored numerous button and badge elements to provide much more premium and crisp contrasting looks. Specifically, I\'ve transitioned yellow and amber text on buttons to white text with vibrant orange backgrounds for the desired \"bubble\" look. I applied this across multiple components, including `Estadisticas.tsx`, `GestionGeneral.tsx`, `EquiposEnviados.tsx`, `Casillero.tsx`, and `CruceSeriales.tsx`, as well as floating history logs. The goal is a more cohesive and modern high-contrast color scheme, overall.\n\n\n**Improving Readability of Metrics**\n\nI\'ve significantly improved the readability of the \"Ingreso de Equipos Entregados\" (and \"Disponibles\") metrics panels. I enlarged the period label to be bolder and lighter, while the counts now use a crisp, bold white sans-serif font. I also updated the download button with a high-contrast orange background and white text, with the \"Disponibles\" counter green. This makes the distinction between the columns exceptionally clear. I also updated the title of the first counter to read \"Disponibles\" with the sub-label \"Cancelado, N#A y Recuperado\" in `Estadisticas.tsx`.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 299505513
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
