  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Adjusting Typefaces**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the user\'s suggestion to improve readability. I\'ve determined that their existing `font-mono` choices in the date fields are problematic, particularly for `fecha salida cliente`, `guia salida cliente`, and destination/dispatch. My new proposal swaps `font-mono` for a sans-serif typeface, using `font-sans font-medium text-white` for clarity.\n\n\n**Refining Readability Adjustments**\n\nI\'ve pushed forward with the font readability adjustments, and implemented the `font-sans` strategy, as discussed. Specifically, I\'ve swapped `font-mono` with `font-sans text-white font-medium` in \"Fecha Salida Cliente\" and \"Gu\303\255a Salida (Cliente)\", also changing \"Destino Despacho\" to `font-sans uppercase text-white font-medium` for consistency and clarity, with Inter font. I\'m now checking for similar instances elsewhere.\n\n\n**Expanding Font Modifications**\n\nI\'m now extending the font adjustments to the \"Casillero\" view, focusing on date and \"salida\" fields within that section. I\'ve also identified the inputs for `serialSustituto` and `fechaSalida` under substitute equipment as candidates for the sans-serif treatment. Specifically, I\'m updating the `className` properties to utilize `font-sans` for improved legibility, aiming for consistency and clarity in these fields.\n\n\n**Reimagining Annual Balance**\n\nI\'m now reimagining the \"Totalizaci\303\263n de Balance Anual\" section, focusing on providing more insightful data. Considering the user\'s feedback, I\'m proposing an \"ANALIZADOR DE STOCK CR\303\215TICO Y CONTROL DE ROTACI\303\223N\" instead. This new section will feature a progress indicator showing overall inventory health through a \"Porcentaje de Entrega\" metric, calculated using serial counts and delivery status. The specific metrics, such as \"Total Seriales\" and \"Total Entregados,\" will be clearly displayed.\n\n\n**Calculating Stock Insights**\n\nI\'m now calculating stock insights, focusing on \"Total Disponibles\" which includes \"CANCELADO\", \"N#A\", and \"SIN ESTATUS\" statuses. I am building a helper block for this. The next step is \"Alertas de Stock por Modelo,\" which involves calculating availability per model, flagging those with critically low availability (less than 3) as \"REABASTECIMIENTO REQUERIDO,\" and adequately stocked items as \"CONTROL SALUDABLE\". I intend to build an interactive tool.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 6
      nanos: 742982921
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
