t, a grid showcases model cards, each with color-coded badges indicating stock status. Download buttons will be integrated elegantly, hopefully on the top. I\'m preparing to rewrite lines 291-338 in `Estadisticas.tsx` with JSX and Tailwind.\n\n\n**Implementing Export Logic**\n\nI\'m now integrating export functionalities. The current focus is on allowing users to export data based on yearly periods and total values. I\'m building this feature so that users have a clear option. I\'m carefully reviewing the logic in `handleExportPeriod` to ensure it works properly, and will output data based on the selected period and scope. I\'m focusing on the annual export, which is key.\n\n\n**Refining Export Interface**\n\nI\'m now putting the finishing touches on the export interface, focusing specifically on user experience. I\'m aiming to make it super clear for exporting annual data and total amounts. I\'ve designed the button\'s layout, ensuring it\'s intuitive and easy for the user. I\'m evaluating the color scheme and text to align perfectly with the overall application\'s design, and will include the necessary code to get the user this functionality.\n\n\n\n**Finalizing Button Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating the export button. I\'m focusing on the visual styling and placement, ensuring it aligns with the application\'s aesthetic. I\'m ensuring it\'s clear for users to find the export function. The button text will be \"EXCEL DISPONIBLES ANUAL\", in uppercase, tracking-wider style and colors. I am placing it within the \"METRICAS DINAMICAS CALCULADAS\" section.\n\n\n**Calculating Stock Efficiency**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on a critical metric: the efficiency of my stock. I\'m focusing on calculating and displaying both \"\303\215ndice de Rotaci\303\263n Activo\" and \"Reserva en Casillero\". The first calculation is: `serials.filter(s => [\'ACTIVO\', \'PENDIENTE\', \'SUSPENDIDO\'].includes(s.status)).length / serials.length) * 100`. The second is `serials.filter(s => s.isCasillero).length / serials.length) * 100`. I\'m also preparing to create progress bars.\n\n\n**Evaluating Recovery Rate**\n\nI\'m now calculating the \"Tasa de Recuperaci\303\263n\" metric, and showing it on screen. I\'m focusing on ensuring its accuracy. I\'m calculating the percent of serials with a status that is \'CANCELADO\', \'N#A\', or \'RECUPERADO\'. I\'m also ensuring the progress bar fills accordingly. I\'m looking at implementing a \"STOCK SALUDABLE\" indicator, which will display the correct status of each model.\n\n\n**Calculating Recovery Rate Display**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the UI for the recovery rate metric. I\'ve successfully calculated and now display the \"Tasa de Recuperaci\303\263n\", and it is showing correctly on screen! I\'m now fine-tuning the progress bar\'s dynamic width, ensuring it accurately reflects the calculated percentage based on the data. I\'m also preparing to create the \"STOCK SALUDABLE\" indicator, which will display the correct status of each model.\n\n\n**Visualizing Model Stock Stats**\n\nI\'m now iterating on model display. I\'m focusing on the UI for displaying the stock of each model, specifically, implementing a design based on the existing code structure. I\'m focusing on key metrics like the total, \"Disponibles\", and \"Entregados\" counts. I\'m aiming to visually represent the status with color-coded badges, especially the critical \"REABASTECER URGENTEMENTE\" alerts.\n\n\n**Refining Badge Logic**\n\nI\'m now refining the color-coded badge logic for model stock status. I\'m focusing on \"Disponibles\", and \"Entregados\" counts and the color-coding badges. I\'m leveraging the existing structure in the existing code, but with more emphasis on the visual representation of \"REABASTECER URGENTEMENTE\" alerts. I\'m making sure critical alerts are bold and clear.\n\n\n"
