    thinking: "**Isolating the Variable**\n\nI\'ve confirmed `emailSerialsArray` is solely used within `CruceSeriales.tsx`. This is great for focusing our efforts! Now, I\'m envisioning a design for that component: it should be visually appealing, highly responsive, and easy to use. The first feature to implement will be the \"Validador (Hoja2)\" functionality.\n\n\n**Designing the UI**\n\nI\'m now sketching out the UI design. I\'m imagining a clean, standard interface for CSV loading. The core will be two side-by-side textareas, one for \"CORREO\" and one for \"F\303\215SICOS\", each with dynamic line counters and placeholders. I\'m focusing on visual cues: matching lines highlighted with icons or solid colors, while unmatched lines are subtly grayed. Finally, a clear \"Cruce Summary\" will display match indicators.\n\n\n**Refining the Action Panel**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the action panel design. I\'ve decided on prominent numeric indicators for match counts and effectiveness rate. Also, I have a clear plan for the \"Add Matches to General Management\" button, including status handling (Validador inheritance or forced state). The Export and Clear buttons are also defined. I\'m focusing on the elegant simplicity of the user interface.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will overwrite `/src/components/CruceSeriales.tsx` with a simplified, highly polished real-time crossing tool. It parses the inputs instantly on every keystroke, showing the matches with active colors and non-matches as gray list items beneath the corresponding textareas without any redundant \"Agregar\" buttons or secondary fields."
    thinking_duration {
