mic, highly visual approach to the two input fields. I\'m imagining a gorgeous, styled box for both \"Correo\" and \"F\303\255sicos\". When populated, these boxes will display serials with clear labels and styled highlighting, showing matches and non-matches. An \"Editar\" or \"Cargar\" button will toggle the underlying textarea for adding or modifying serials. I\'m exploring the idea of showing the text area by default, but I need to make it extremely user-friendly. I\'m taking the prior feedback into consideration.\n\n\n**Clarifying Input Strategy**\n\nI\'m now completely aligned with the two-panel structure: \"Seriales desde Correo\" and \"Seriales F\303\255sicos.\" The core idea is that each panel will function as a single interactive list/editor, replacing the separate textarea and display. I envision the pasting and scanning workflows happening within these two fields, with real-time matching and highlighting directly within the text as the crucial feedback mechanism. I\'m focusing on the technical feasibility and optimal UX for this design.\n\n\n**Implementing Input Switching**\n\nI\'ve refined the design to feature a seamless transition between input and visual list modes within each of the two fields. Initially, an empty container displays a standard textarea for pasting or typing serials. Once input is provided and focus is lost, or a \"Procesar\" / \"Listo\" action is triggered, the field dynamically switches to the \"Interactive Match list\" state. This mode showcases the serials visually, with highlighting indicating matches and graying out non-matches. An \"Editar / Pistolear\" button facilitates easy return to the textarea for further modifications. I am moving towards automatically switching to the visual state on focus loss.\n\n\n**Defining Interactive Inputs**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the dynamic interaction within each panel. I envision the \"Correo\" and \"F\303\255sicos\" panels offering persistent serial list displays with inline input. An always-present, unobtrusive input field will allow seamless barcode scanning or manual entry, even when viewing the serials. I\'m also including a button to toggle a textarea for mass-editing or pasting, allowing the user to paste or edit in bulk.\n\n\n"
