  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Examining Serial Statuses**\n\nI\'m currently focused on how to manage status changes for serial numbers within the physical list (`seriales fisicos (lectora)`). I\'ve discovered the `fisicoText` field stores a delimited list of serial numbers, separated by newlines, commas, or semicolons. My next step is to figure out how custom-edited or \"other\" statuses are currently stored or managed for these serials.\n\n\n**Considering Status Sources**\n\nI\'m now grappling with where to store and manage the statuses of these serial numbers. I\'ve re-evaluated the requirement: users need to edit statuses (\"CANCELADO\", \"N#A\", etc.) within the \"seriales fisicos (lectora)\" field. These serials don\'t inherently have statuses, except if they can be validated within the master dataset (`datosMaestro`). The question is, should I dynamically update the database, use a local state map (like `customStatuses`), or modify the existing loaded status within the \"datosMaestro\"?\n\n\n**Analyzing Status Logic**\n\nI\'ve been examining the existing code, specifically `lookupValidador` and `getStatusBadgeStyle`, to understand how serial numbers and statuses are handled. It seems `lookupValidador` searches the `datosMaestro` array and the found item\'s serial number. The `getStatusBadgeStyle` function appears to determine the visual styling of status badges. Currently, I\'m focusing on why the user wants to replace the orange text within orange bubbles, and how that can be accomplished.\n\n\n**Investigating Color Overrides**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics of the orange bubble color and white text request. I\'ve pinpointed the relevant CSS classes: `bg-orange-500/10 border-orange-500/30 text-orange-400`, as well as where a white text option exists. Further, I\'m examining how the current styling logic for those colors is defined within the `getStatusBadgeStyle` function, and if any of those orange-based styles need override. I believe the code shows where the \'\342\234\223 MATCH\' text can be white inside the orange bubble. I need to determine if an orange style with white text needs to be added, or is already present.\n\n\n**Refining Color Options**\n\nI\'ve been exploring how to achieve white text within the orange status bubbles. I\'ve identified the CSS classes controlling the styling and considered modifications. Changing `text-orange-400` to `text-slate-100` or `text-white` in the existing style, `bg-orange-500/10 border-orange-500/30 text-orange-400`, seems promising. I\'m also thinking we can create a nice look with something similar to `text-white bg-orange-500/20 border-orange-500/30`. I\'m now considering the best method to enable singular or grouped status editing for each serial. I\'m currently assessing UI options for status editing when in \"visual\" mode.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 7
      nanos: 307750555
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
