  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Completing the Logo**\n\nI\'ve finished the logo enlargement, and I\'m quite pleased with the professional look. Now, I\'m shifting focus to the `CruceSeriales.tsx` component features. Specifically, I\'m diving into the \"physical serials\" reader field. I am figuring out how to make each serial bubble editable for status updates after clicking the \"ready\" button.\n\n\n**Adjusting Color Schemes**\n\nI\'ve homed in on the orange color issue within the serial bubbles. The key lies in the `text-orange-400` class within the \"match container style.\" By replacing this with `text-slate-100` or `text-white`, the orange text within the matching serial boxes will turn white. I am making these changes now.\n\n\n**Refining Visual Contrast**\n\nI\'ve been examining the color contrast of the serial bubbles, specifically the text and status labels. Replacing `text-orange-400` with `text-slate-100` in the match container style is working well for serial text clarity. I\'m now looking at the badge style and testing what `text-white` might look like.\n\n\n**Implementing State Selectors**\n\nI\'m now integrating inline `<select>` dropdowns into the serial bubbles within the visual display, to allow for individual status updates on each physical serial item. I\'ll need to use those values. I can see the dropdowns being extremely easy to implement, let\'s keep going.\n\n\n**Designing Status Controls**\n\nI am now designing the inline `<select>` element for status updates within each serial bubble, with options for `\"CANCELADO\"`, `\"N#A\"`, `\"RECUPERADO\"`, etc. My logic is that user selections will directly update the status in the `datosMaestro` data structure through the `updateSerialStatus` function. I am working on the function right now.\n\n\n**Enabling Bulk Actions**\n\nI\'ve got the individual serial status updates working, and now I\'m expanding it! I\'m adding a group status assignment feature. My plan is to include a bulk action bar, maybe just above the physical serials visual list. This will allow for setting a specific status for multiple serials with one click. I\'ll design a nice toolbar for this. It will be neat!\n\n\n**Adding Bulk Actions**\n\nI\'m now implementing the bulk action bar above the serial visuals, with a dropdown to set statuses for all entries. I\'ve got the basic structure set. I\'m focusing on the logic to confirm the bulk update, and then the actual data changes within the state management. The user confirmation will be implemented.\n\n\n**Confirming Bulk Updates**\n\nI\'m now diving into the logic for confirming and applying bulk updates to the serial statuses. The function iterates through the selected serials, updating their statuses in a copy of the existing data, and handling cases where serials are new or already present. It\'s working well. I\'m focusing on ensuring data integrity with this strategy.\n\n\n**Refining Match Indicators**\n\nI\'m now integrating an \"isMatch\" indicator into each serial bubble, displaying either \"\342\234\223 MATCH\" or \"SIN MATCH\". I\'m also ensuring the text color contrasts appropriately based on the match status. I am working on the select dropdown styling to be standard. I am integrating these display logic elements now!\n\n\n**Optimizing Data Handling**\n\nI\'m now integrating logic for the dropdown options to directly call `updateSerialStatus(serial, selectValue)`. This means state updates happen immediately upon selection. It streamlines the status updates within each serial bubble, which is key to the design goal.\n\n\n**Implementing Local Storage**\n\nI\'ve integrated local storage persistence, ensuring all state changes trigger a re-render and are saved. I\'ve also swapped `text-orange-400` with `text-white` to update the orange text in the physical serial list, achieving better visual contrast. Additionally, I\'m updating the status badge style to feature white text inside orange status bubbles.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 13
      nanos: 479333535
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
