    started_at {
      seconds: 1779660693
      nanos: 568749976
    }
  }
  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining UI Aesthetics**\n\nI\'ve been working on refining the user interface aesthetics. Specifically, I\'m replacing all instances of dark orange bubbles and overlays. My current approach involves implementing a softer pastel orange in their place, specifically using the following Tailwind CSS classes: `bg-orange-400/25 border-orange-300/30 text-orange-200`.\n\n\n**Prioritizing White Text**\n\nI\'ve decided that all serial text, whether digital or physical, needs to be pure white for maximum visual precision. I\'m focusing on ensuring this text is clear, uppercase, and monospaced for optimal readability. I also think I should completely remove that on-page \"Asignaci\303\263n de Estado Grupal\" dropdown. It\'s time to build a modal with a status selector.\n\n\n**Implementing Modal Enhancements**\n\nI\'m now integrating a \"A\303\261adir a Gesti\303\263n General\" button at the bottom of the modal, allowing users to directly commit matched items to the general system. The plan is to ensure users can easily set statuses and push selections. I am also working to streamline the Reconciliation settings. Specifically, I am removing the \"PENDIENTE\" and \"ACTIVO\" status buttons from the \"Forzar Estado al Reconciliar\" options, to simplify the interface.\n\n\n**Simplifying Excel Input**\n\nI\'m removing the Excel file validator in favor of an \"**IMS**\" button. Clicking this will open a modal with \"SERIAL TERMINAL\" and \"STATUS SERVICIO\" textareas, capable of handling over 100,000 lines copied from Excel. Data alignment is crucial, with each line in \"SERIAL TERMINAL\" corresponding to the same line in \"STATUS SERVICIO.\" On confirmation, the app parses the data into `datosMaestro`, defaulting any missing IMS serials to `N#A` and its category `DISPONIBLE`. I need to ensure that the parsing is graceful.\n\n\n**Optimizing Data Lookup**\n\nI\'m now focusing on optimizing the data lookup process within `CruceSeriales.tsx`. My current plan is to replace the existing `.find()` array operations with a `Map` (or potentially an object dictionary) for the `datosMaestro` lookup. This should provide instantaneous O(1) lookups instead of the current O(N) performance, which is essential to avoid browser freezing with so many entries. I\'ll need to do a clean index-based loop.\n\n\n"
