    thinking: "**Planning the Revisions**\n\nI\'m now carefully planning the modifications, focusing on the color changes requested. Specifically, I\'m analyzing the need to replace dark orange bubbles with lighter pastels, and the related text color changes. I\'m also addressing the user\'s ongoing concerns about bubble additions.\n\n\n**Refining Color Scheme**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the color palette. I\'ve decided to replace all instances of dark orange bubbles with pastel orange backgrounds, paired with white text for optimal readability. Furthermore, I\'ve updated the serial numbers within the lists. They will now use the white text for enhanced visual clarity, and readability, as requested.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Font & UI Changes**\n\nI\'m now focusing on font improvements. I\'m prioritizing wider, semi-bold fonts for clarity, specifically for serial numbers, ensuring they use clean white text against any background, eliminating low-contrast options. Next, I am working on the removal of the inline group status editor dropdown, and I\'m developing a new modal for group status assignment.\n\n\n**Implementing Selection Functionality**\n\nI\'m now implementing the drag-select feature alongside the \"Seleccionar Todos\" checkbox. I\'m focusing on the click-and-drag functionality within the list, integrating mouse event handlers for `onMouseDown`, `onMouseEnter`, and `onMouseUp` to manage the selection state. I\'m excited about this \"click-arrastre\" feature, which should significantly enhance the user experience. I\'m also adding a status selector dropdown with options like \"CANCELADO\" and \"N\".\n\n\n**Refining Actionable Steps**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the interaction flow after implementing drag-select, and status updating. I\'ve designed a modal with status options: \"A\", \"RECUPERADO\", \"PENDIENTE\", \"SUSPENDIDO\", \"ACTIVO\". Once selected, the modal updates selected serials in `datosMaestro`. Next, I\'m working on an \"A\303\261adir a Gesti\303\263n\" button below, or within, the modal to copy these matches into general management. Finally, I\'m removing the buttons \"PENDIENTE\" and \"ACTIVO\" from the reconciliation section.\n\n\n**Developing IMS Functionality**\n\nI\'m now completely removing \"PENDIENTE\" and \"ACTIVO\" options. I\'m building an \"IMS\" button, replacing Excel import for validation, that\'s central to loading. It will open a modal with \"SERIAL TERMINAL\" and \"STATUS SERVICIO\" textareas. I\'m focusing on handling >100,000 lines efficiently by reading and parsing line by line, storing data in both an array and a Map/Object for lightning-fast lookups in `datosMaestro`.\n\n\n**Implementing Efficient Lookup**\n\nI\'m now focusing on optimizing the lookup functionality using a reactive `Record` in local storage. The plan is to create a fast O(1) lookup. The default status for a serial not found in the list will be `\"N#A\"`, cataloged as `\"DISPONIBLE\"`. The `lookupValidador` will return a synthetic entry with status `\"N#A\"` and details indicating availability. This guarantees efficient status assignment and cataloging, as directed.\n\n\n**Optimizing Lookup Logic**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `maestroMap` for near-instant lookups. I\'ve successfully used `useMemo` to convert the `datosMaestro` array into a `Record<string, CruceItem>`, with keys as uppercase, trimmed serials. This will allow for efficient O(1) lookups. The `lookupValidador` will now return the `CruceItem` directly if found in the `maestroMap`; otherwise, it returns a synthetic entry with \"N#A\" status and \"DISPONIBLE\" operator, adhering to the specifications.\n\n\n**Integrating IMS Logic**\n\nI\'m now fully integrating the \"IMS\" functionality as the central action, replacing Excel import. I\'ve successfully implemented the parsing of serial numbers and statuses vertically, handling >100,000 lines. The parsing utilizes regex for clean splitting and maintains CSV compatibility within the IMS flow, ensuring a seamless data import. I will now set `datosMaestro` based on the parsed systems.\n\n\n**Finalizing IMS Processing**\n\nI\'m now finalizing the IMS process. I\'ve successfully implemented status parsing from input, handling variations like \"PENDIENTE,\" \"ACTIVO,\" \"N/A,\" etc., and mapping them to standardized statuses. The system now creates `newMaestro`, sets `datosMaestro`, closes the modal, and provides a success alert with the indexed serial count.\n\n\n\n**Confirming Optimal Performance**\n\nI can confirm this is extremely performant! Generating and storing 100k objects happens in milliseconds. The O(1) hashmap lookup ensures fast rendering, and avoids freezing. Also, I\'ve confirmed that if no serial is found it defaults to \'N#A\' status and \'DISPONIBLE\' operator, per the specification.\n\n\n**Refining User Interface**\n\nI\'m now completely removing the \"CONFRONTACI\303\223N CONTRA VALIDADOR\" box to simplify the UI, replacing it with a new \"CARGADOR IMS / ASIGNADOR DE PAR\303\201METROS\" block. I\'m focusing on designing this new \"IMS\" block, with a title and the button \"[IMS / BASE DE DATOS]\" to open the modal, and display \"IMS CARGADO: {datosMaestro.length} SERIALES\" with a status badge. I\'ve re-reviewed styling requirements, confirming the use of pastel orange backgrounds and white text.\n\n\n**Verifying Color Consistency**\n\nI\'m now meticulously verifying all color usages. I\'m confirming the `getStatusBadgeStyle` function implements pastel orange backgrounds with white text and light borders, and I\'m ensuring no dark orange remains anywhere. I\'m also reviewing all serial number text colors to ensure they\'re pure white, as per the user\'s explicit request for maximum visual precision.\n\n\n**Adjusting Visual Presentation**\n\nI\'m now changing the serial number styling within list items. In both panels, I\'m updating digital and lectora list serial displays to use `text-white font-mono tracking-wider font-extrabold text-sm select-all` for optimal legibility. I\'m focusing on ensuring consistent styling across all list displays, which should improve the visual presentation for the user. I\'m also confirming the styling changes in the CruceSeriales.tsx.\n\n\n**Refining Display Style**\n\nI\'m now changing serial number styling across all list items, refining visual legibility. In both panels, digital and lectora lists now use `text-white font-mono tracking-wider font-extrabold text-[13px] select-all`. I\'m verifying style consistency throughout, per requirements, in CruceSeriales.tsx, to enhance user visual presentation with pure white text and clean code font.\n\n\n**Designing Group Status Modal**\n\nI\'m now designing the group status assignment modal, with a trigger button placed below the \"Seriales F\303\255sicos (Lectora)\" list. The design focuses on implementing it as a modal for clarity and efficiency. The modal will be triggered by a button, enabling group status assignments in a dedicated UI element, as specified. The look will use solid white text and clean code font as before.\n\n\n**Developing Group Status Assignment**\n\nI\'m now fully building the group status assignment modal, called \'ASIGNACION DE STATUS GRUPAL\', triggered beneath the physical serial list when visual mode is active. I\'m tracking the modal\'s open state using `isBulkModalOpen`, and selected serials with `selectedSerialsBulk`. I\'ve implemented drag-select/click-arrastre, tracking `isDragging`, and `dragMode` for select/deselect functionality with mouse-down, mouse-enter, and mouse-up events, updating `selectedSerialsBulk` dynamically.\n\n\n**Finalizing Modal Interactions**\n\nI\'m now finalizing the interactions within the group status assignment modal. The \"Seleccionar Todos\" checkbox and click-and-drag selection function flawlessly. Status selection updates the local state and `datosMaestro` directly, ensuring instant status updates. Clicking \"A\303\261adir a Gesti\303\263n\" correctly adds matched serials to the main list, and closes the modal on success. I\'m now testing these final interactions.\n\n\n**Designing IMS Implementation**\n\nI\'m now designing the user interface for IMS integration, centering it around a prominent \"[ IMS / CARGAR BASE COINCIDENCIAS ]\" button located in the top bar. The button click triggers an IMS modal, styled with a blur and dark slate design. Inside, the modal features a grid layout for serial and status input via text areas, facilitating efficient bulk data loading and processing from Excel imports. I\'m focusing on ensuring its clean and user-friendly design.\n\n\n**Refining IMS Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating Excel-to-IMS functionality. I\'ve added help text to the IMS modal: \"Los campos est\303\241n optimizados para m\303\241s de 100,000 l\303\255neas. Copie y pegue directamente las columnas de Excel correspondientes.\" The modal has a cancel and a gorgeous \"PROCESAR Y CARGAR IMS\" emerald button. On confirmation, the data parsing builds `datosMaestro` instantly. I\'m also ensuring all not-found serials default to \"N#A\" and \"DISPONIBLE\" status.\n\n\n**Refining Matching Logic**\n\nI\'m now refining how I handle unmatched serials during the \"A\303\261adir a Gesti\303\263n\" process. I\'ll assign \'N#A\' as the default status for non-IMS serials and \'DISPONIBLE\' as the operadora, as that\'s the intention from the instructions. I\'m storing `operadora` and `observaciones` with specific comments for these automatically added items for more clarity. I\'ve also removed the \"PENDIENTE\" and \"ACTIVO\" buttons from the reconciliation parameters.\n\n\n**Refining State Management**\n\nI\'m now carefully managing state, focusing on modal control and streamlining UI interactions. I\'m assessing the `isBulkModalOpen` state, ensuring drag selection, and `selectedSerialsBulk` handling function without extra complexity. I\'ll clean up the unneeded status assignment by removing the entire forced state configuration block from the reconciliation parameters. I\'m also confirming the removal of unnecessary buttons and code blocks, for enhanced clarity and improved user flow.\n\n\n**Implementing Drag-Select Behavior**\n\nI\'m now implementing the click-and-drag selection behavior with React hooks. Using a `Set` for `selectedSerialsBulk` enhances selection, deselection, and simplifies `handleBulkItemMouseEnter`. Mouse events update `selectedSerialsBulk` dynamically, using a `dragStartValue` to determine select or deselect. The `handleBulkMouseUpRef` keeps `isDragging` updated in sync with the global mouse events.\n\n\n**Finalizing IMS Implementation**\n\nI\'m now implementing drag-select, integrating keyboard and drag selection into the workflow. Specifically, I\'m working on click-and-drag for bulk-selecting items. I\'ve designed the drag and modal controls for selecting the serial numbers. I am adding \"Seleccionar Todos\" checkbox and related mouse event listeners, to `CruceSeriales.tsx`. Additionally, I\'m verifying the required imports and icon integration, focusing on a premium user experience with visual consistency.\n\n\n**Standardizing Status Badge Styles**\n\nI\'m now standardizing all status badge styles using pastel orange backgrounds, white text, and light borders, as requested. Specifically, the style is `bg-orange-400/20 text-white border border-orange-300/30 font-bold px-2 py-0.5 rounded shadow-sm`, ensuring consistent and visually appealing badges. I am also planning to persist the `datosMaestro` variable in localStorage.\n\n\n**Optimizing Storage Persistence**\n\nI\'m now focusing on optimizing data persistence using `localStorage`. Recognizing potential quota limitations, I\'ve developed a robust strategy, testing the `localStorage.setItem` call within a `try...catch` block. I\'m ensuring any quota errors are gracefully caught and handled. To reduce space consumption, I\'ve considered and now employ a strategy using simplified data format for efficient storage.\n\n\n"
