    modified_response: "I have successfully resolved the issue causing duplicate React keys during serial additions.\n\n### What Was the Issue?\nThe duplicate key error (`1779661161777` + decimal random part) was caused by a standard JavaScript floating-point precision limitation. Combining `Date.now()` with `Math.random()` synchronously inside loops resulted in identical values due to the limited precision of floating-point numbers when representing very large integers (millisecond timestamps). Under high-speed execution within loops, multiple elements were rounded to the exact same ID, causing duplicate key warnings in the React renderer.\n\n### How Was It Solved?\nWe replaced all collision-prone ID generators with guaranteed high-precision sequential IDs across the application:\n1. **CSV Upload Engine**: Updated imports to assign `Date.now() * 1000 + index` to any entries missing pre-defined IDs, maintaining full uniqueness.\n2. **Batch Item Addition**: Upgraded the manual/barcode loader map loops to leverage loop index offsets, ensuring entirely safe sequential integer keys.\n3. **Cross-Referencing Tool (Cruce)**: Configured matched item ingestion loops to integrate safe `Date.now() * 1000 + matchIdx` ID generators, completely eliminating duplicate children key errors across updates."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
