    thinking: "**Analyzing the Bug**\n\nI\'m now investigating the broken \"Limpiar campos\" button in Cruce de Seriales. I\'m focusing on the `limpiarTodo` implementation within `src/components/CruceSeriales.tsx`. My current reading is focused in finding a potential coding logic error. I\'m digging into its associated code to determine why it\'s not clearing fields as expected. I\'m looking for the cause.\n\n\n**Pinpointing the Culprit**\n\nI\'ve zeroed in on the `limpiarTodo` function. It seems the issue stems from `window.confirm`. I\'m starting to think the iFrame environment is the culprit, as its restrictions are mentioned in the docs. The `useEffect` hook, while seemingly relevant, appears less directly involved in the immediate failure. The `localStorage` interactions are behaving as expected, but the prompt\'s behavior in an iFrame is now my prime suspect.\n\n\n**Refactoring the UI**\n\nI\'m now shifting gears to the UI. The stale confirmation dialog is out; I\'m planning a custom modal or a state-based approach. I\'m also ready to ditch alerts and confirmations, favouring immediate feedback. This approach should bypass iFrame limitations. I\'m prioritizing direct action or on-screen tags that don\'t block execution.\n\nI\'m also working on aesthetic improvements to the interface. I\'m targeting the pale orange tones and plan to use vibrant orange, like `bg-orange-500` or `text-orange-500`, for a more impactful look, and pure white for serial texts. The IMS button will become green with white text.\n\n\n**Updating the IMS Look**\n\nI\'m now overhauling the IMS button\'s appearance, aiming for a strong green aesthetic. I\'ll use `bg-emerald-600 hover:bg-emerald-500 text-white` for a vibrant, solid feel, or `bg-green-600 hover:bg-green-500 text-white` as an alternate. Also, I\'m removing the database description, as instructed. Finally, I\'m making the MATCH indicator in both Cruce de Seriales fields (Correo & Lectora) a flashy green, with white text, and removing the pulsing effect.\n\n\n**Refining the UI**\n\nI\'m now focusing on UI adjustments for enhanced clarity and aesthetics. I\'m prioritizing making the MATCH indicators in the fields visually striking with bold green backgrounds and white text. I\'m also addressing font legibility across buttons, planning to implement a consistent, professional font style, likely matching Inter, which I see is the guide\'s recommendation. I\'m also looking into increasing the size of main menu icons to improve their visibility. Finally, I\'m starting work on the \"DISGLOBAL TRACKING\" logo, aiming for a minimalist yellow-accented design.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 6
      nanos: 262581432
    }
