    thinking: "**Interpreting User Intent**\n\nI\'ve determined there\'s no existing image file, so generation is the likely goal. Based on the user\'s provided context - I\'ve just observed a dark blue \"D\" character in the uploaded image, and it seems this is what is desired for a generated logo.\n\n\n**Evaluating Generation Options**\n\nI\'m now weighing the best approach: generating a new image versus creating an SVG. The user\'s request for a replacement logo that \"glows\" and matches the style of the existing PNG makes SVG generation particularly appealing, as it offers precise control over visual effects like glow and scalability. I\'ve also noted the user\'s explicit instructions for \"DISGLOBAL TRACKING\" to be redesigned.\n\n\n**Refining SVG Design**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on an SVG approach, inspired by the App.tsx code. It looks like the glowing effect of the original logo comes from a pulsing background and subtle styling, not the icon itself. I\'m focusing on crafting a high-fidelity inline SVG of a stylized, rounded \"D\". The plan is for a deep dark blue-grey color, allowing for the precise glowing effect to be applied through inline styles or Tailwind classes, ensuring scalability and control.\n\n\n**Prioritizing SVG Detail**\n\nMy latest thought is to integrate a payment POS terminal inside the \"D\" character, complete with a credit card slot, card insertion, and a printing paper roll with a barcode. I also envision a golden-orange arrow cutting through the \"D\", symbolizing growth. I\'m leaning heavily towards an SVG with glowing effects and responsive Tailwind classes to ensure a polished design. Alternatively, I\'m generating an image using `generate_image`. It may be best to craft an SVG in React.\n\n\n**Addressing UI Issues**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the user\'s feedback concerning the \"limpiar campos\" button within `CruceSeriales.tsx`. My current thought is to bypass `window.confirm` to resolve its responsiveness issues inside the iframe. Instead, I\'ll directly clear the state or implement a temporary success indicator. I\'m also ensuring the correct inputs are cleared, including `emailText` and `fisicoText`, and that the view mode resets to `\'edit\'`. I\'ll also replace pastel oranges with vibrant hues like `bg-orange-500/20 text-white border-orange-500`.\n\n\n**Updating UI Elements**\n\nMy current focus is on enhancing the UI\'s visual cues. I\'m updating the IMS button to a vibrant green, incorporating bold white text and a shadow for emphasis. The MATCH indicator will become a striking, easily identifiable green with white letters across both panels. I also plan to remove the specified text from CruceSeriales.tsx and improve button fonts across the board for increased readability and a more professional look.\n\n\n"
