  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Visualizing New Design**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the visual redesign of \"DISGLOBAL TRACKING.\" I\'m prioritizing the color scheme: \"DISGLOBAL\" in yellow, \"TRACKING\" in electric blue. I\'m also planning to replace the current glowing icon with the attached PNG, ensuring it maintains the same style and glowing effect.\n\n\n**Analyzing Icon Design**\n\nI\'ve reviewed the uploaded image and am now integrating its visual elements into the existing design. Specifically, I\'m focusing on incorporating the dark slate-blue \"D\" and the card reader with the gold-yellow arrow. I\'m considering how to best replace the current network icon in `App.tsx` (lines 299-310) with this new graphic, while retaining the desired glow and style.\n\n\n**Crafting Detailed SVG**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into creating a high-fidelity SVG. My focus is on rendering the design elements precisely: a stylized, rounded dark slate-blue \"D\", a light-grey and dark steel-blue POS terminal within it (complete with a credit card and receipt), and a golden-orange arrow. I\'m aiming for the `w-32 h-32` dimensions and plan to implement the `animate-pulse` class for the glow.\n\n\n**Implementing SVG Component**\n\nI\'m now writing an SVG component, `LogoIcon`, to replace the glowing logo. My approach involves using SVG paths for precise rendering. I\'m focusing on defining a gradient for a brilliant \"D\" and incorporating shadows and gradients to achieve a premium, vibrant feel. I\'m working with the colors \"F59E0B\" and \"FBBF24\" for the arrow. I\'ll maintain the glow effect using CSS classes.\n\n\n**Refining Glow Effects**\n\nI\'m now iterating on the glow effect and backdrop. I\'m focusing on defining gradients for both the \"D\" and considering a backdrop shadow for depth. My current SVG includes a backdrop shadow, a dark steel-blue \"D\", and a steel-grey POS terminal. I\'m specifically exploring `feGaussianBlur` and `feComposite` for the glow.\n\n\n**Detailing POS Terminal**\n\nI\'m now deep in the details, refining the POS terminal\'s appearance within the SVG. I\'m focusing on the keypad layout, precisely positioning and styling the rectangles to create a grid-like effect on the screen. I\'m leveraging transformations to ensure the keypad aligns correctly with the rotated terminal.\n\n\n**Finalizing Receipt Details**\n\nI\'m now putting the finishing touches on the receipt component within the SVG. I\'ve added a pair of rectangles and I am now fine-tuning the receipt details. This includes the paper roll, some barcode lines, and their positioning relative to the POS terminal, and the correct styling to ensure the design is ready for use.\n\n\n**Polishing Visual Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating the credit card and the golden-orange arrow into the SVG. I\'ve successfully placed the credit card and receipt. I\'m focusing on the dynamic, swooping arrow now. I\'m using curved paths and aiming for a clean, premium visual aesthetic. I\'m focusing on precise positioning.\n\n\n**Integrating Visual Styles**\n\nI\'ve made significant progress! The SVG is shaping up perfectly now, matching the image impeccably. I\'m focusing on incorporating high-contrast yellow-orange and electric-blue accents for that premium, sharp look. I\'m also now building the SVG component within React, for that sleek, native, glowing effect in the UI, and integrating these elements, and the proposed text, using the provided example as a model.\n\n\n**Adjusting Button Icons**\n\nI\'m now shifting gears to the main menu buttons. It seems the icons are a bit small; line 453 in `/src/App.tsx` has `size={13}`. I\'ll increase that to `size={18}` or `size={19}` for better legibility. Also, I\'ll update button text fonts to `font-sans font-bold tracking-wider` for a professional, easily readable look.\n\n\n"
