    thinking: "**Analyzing Color Corrections**\n\nI\'m currently focused on color corrections within specific email and reader contexts. I\'m aiming for white text for the \"METRICAS DEL CRUCE Y SALIDA DE CONTROL\" section, matching the \"correccion de colores\" concept, with a vibrant orange field specifically for the reader-only section. I\'m also considering the implications for unique serial totals.\n\n\n**Refining Color Specifications**\n\nI\'ve specified that the \"Coinciden (Match)\" field should be vivid green only in email contexts. For reader contexts, I\'m now setting the \"Solo en Lectora\" field to a bright orange background, and now the text will be white for perfect contrast. Labels and their corresponding numbers are now designated as white for optimal readability across contexts.\n\n\n**Updating Color Codes**\n\nI\'ve shifted focus to the \"Solo en Correo\" field, now implementing the electric blue color as requested. I\'ve switched the background to `#2563EB` with a border of `#3B82F6` for a cleaner look, and the text is now white. This change enhances the contrast for email contexts, while retaining the orange theme for the reader views.\n\n\n**Adjusting Color Schemes**\n\nI\'ve just updated the \"Coinciden (Match)\" field. I\'ve set it to a vivid green background (`#16A34A`), with a matching border of `#22C55E`, and white text for high contrast, enhancing readability. The change also applies a shadow for a sleeker look. I also styled \"Total Serales \303\232nicos\" with a dark background for strong contrast and high elegance.\n\n\n"
