  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing UI Element**\n\nI\'ve been examining the `CruceSeriales.tsx` component, focusing on the Trash2 icon. I noticed only one instance of it exists. I\'ve now shifted my attention to the button element itself, exploring its properties and associated functionality, specifically the `onClick` event and class names.\n\n\n**Investigating Interaction Behavior**\n\nI\'m now diving into the user interaction logic, specifically the behavior when users interact with the text fields and the \"Procesar y Hacer Match\" button. I\'ve observed that inputting text into \"Seriales del Correo (Lista)\" and \"Seriales F\303\255sicos (Lectora)\" triggers a switch to visual view mode, which I confirmed with the conditional render. Clearing the text fields also empties the visual list, which makes sense. I\'ve also uncovered an inconsistency: clearing all inputs doesn\'t automatically revert the view mode to \'edit\', which is an aspect I want to understand better. I\'m checking `limpiarTodo`.\n\n\n**Clarifying Clearing Logic**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the \"Limpiar Campos\" functionality. I\'ve realized that the `setEmailViewMode` and `setFisicoViewMode` states are indeed set to \'edit\' as expected. However, I\'m now exploring if the lists of processed serials (email/physical) are cleared correctly, which are handled by `fisicoText` and `emailText`. I\'m also now digging into how state updates affect the component\'s re-render, especially with respect to the `localStorage` interactions. I\'ve noted down the state declaration for them, and if this is a possible cause for unexpected behavior.\n\n\n**Refining Clearing Functionality**\n\nI\'m now investigating the \"Limpiar Campos\" button\'s placement and behavior. I\'ve found it\'s conditionally rendered, appearing only when the serial lists are empty. This is problematic. My current thought is to ensure the global button is always visible or add individual \"Limpiar\" buttons within each column. I\'m focusing on the `limpiarTodo` function to identify what it actually clears. Lines 745-775 of `CruceSeriales.tsx` are of interest and, specifically, I am now checking lines 707-743. I am going to see if the rendering condition of the `Limpiar Campos` button can be changed, since it would be useful when the inputs are not empty.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 4
      nanos: 720918059
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
