  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the Logo Shape**\n\nI\'m now focused on reproducing the brand logo. I\'ve broken down its key visual elements. I\'m starting with the deep blue, Capital \"D\" shape and the gray shape that completes the bottom contour. I\'m noting specific color codes for precision.\n\n\n**Adding the Golden Arrow**\n\nI\'ve moved on to the iconic golden arrow now. I\'m focusing on reproducing its swooping curve and sharp arrowhead, paying close attention to gradients and shading. I\'m aiming for `#f0a424`, `#f3b735`, or `#f9c83c` for accurate color representation. I\'m also preparing for the animation component, now. My goal is to use SVG\'s internal `<style>` or CSS classes to create a sequential glow effect \342\200\223 arrow first, then POS screen.\n\n\n**Sequencing the Animation**\n\nI\'ve just structured the animation timeline. I\'ve broken down a 5-second cycle into stages. The arrow\'s glow will be active for the first 35%, then dormant. The screen highlight begins dormant, then blooms neon green from 50% to 85%, and finally fades back to normal. I\'m focusing on the animation of CSS classes now.\n\n\n**Mapping the Visual Elements**\n\nI\'m now precisely mapping the logo\'s coordinates. I\'m focusing on the \"D\" now: the vertical navy block (`#1b3147`), the horizontal and upper curve, and the lower gray curve (`#464e54`). I\'m noting the gap in the curve where the arrow passes. The arrow starts at the bottom curve, and sweeps upwards. The POS device is next, with its slate grey case, dark charcoal screen, and keypad, and is rotated 28-30 degrees counter-clockwise.\n\n\n**Constructing the POS Scene**\n\nI\'m now integrating the POS device with the card insertion and receipt elements. I\'m focusing on the details: metallic keypad keys, the status overlay, and the paper receipt feed, which includes printed lines representing a barcode. I\'m aiming for high fidelity to construct a responsive SVG precisely, now. I am also checking against the background colors, so the colors will pop elegantly against the dark app layout. I have double-checked the color codes to ensure accuracy, and am now drafting the code for `LogoIcon`.\n\n\n"
